{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Collection Item","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404024","type":"Type"}],"id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/library/7762","identified_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"call number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300311706"}],"content":"PR4851 1900","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"repository number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404621"}],"content":"7762","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"preferred term","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404670"}],"content":"The poems of Rudyard Kipling  ","type":"Name"}],"produced_by":{"carried_out_by":[{"_label":"Kipling, Rudyard,","id":"actor/kipling-rudyard","type":"Actor"},{"_label":"A.L. Burt Co.","id":"actor/a-l-burt-co","type":"Actor"}],"timespan":{"_label":"1900","begin_of_the_begin":"1900-01-01T00:00:00Z","end_of_the_end":"1900-01-01T00:00:00Z","type":"TimeSpan"},"type":"Production"},"referred_to_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"inscription statement","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435414"}],"content":"Clipping from unknown source glued to t.p. verso, undated : Tis easy to be pleasant. / When life flows along like a song: / But the man worth while / Is the one who will smile / When everything goes dead wrong. / For the test of the heart is trouble / And it always comes with the years: / And the smile that is worth / The praise of the earth / Is the smile that comes through tears.|grl copy : poor condition.|Inscription on front loose endpaper from L.P. [W]alstorm to Georgia O'Keeffe : Georgia O'Keeffe / With the affectionate regard of her friend / L.P. Walstorm / June 8th, 1912.","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"description statement","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"}],"content":"From Georgia O'Keeffe's Ghost Ranch library.","type":"LinguisticObject"}],"representation":[],"type":"HumanMadeObject"}